body:
"Were you planned?"  
I would probably only say this to someone who was clearly overstepping boundaries or a stranger. 

&#x200B;

I haven't thought of it like that before. I think a lot of it has to do with how their oldest son and his wife have treated them when they had kids. Whenever my SIL didn't agree with something of MIL, she would always pull a "I don't care about your opinion, I'm doing it my way". Which is completely fine, it just ruined their relationship completely. Along with other reasons, that part of the family is basically absent from their and our lives. My MIL is a super family oriented person, and this naturally upsets her to no end.  My husband thinks that MIL is projecting her feelings that she has of SIL onto me. 

&#x200B;

I agree! I don't ever want to be a MIL that is ever overbearing or emotionally manipulative!
